<BaseLayout title="About OilerBilt Home Remodeling" description="Meet OilerBilt Home Remodeling, serving Houston and southwest Harris County with practical residential and commercial remodeling."><div class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><p class="eyebrow">About OilerBilt</p><h1>A remodeling company built around the work.</h1><p>OilerBilt serves homeowners and businesses across Houston and southwest Harris County.</p></div></div><article class="article wrap"><h2>Plain answers before the dust starts</h2><p>Remodeling decisions get expensive when the scope is vague. OilerBilt starts with the existing condition, the result the customer needs and the access or material decisions that affect the work. The confirmed services are kitchen and bathroom remodeling, drywall installation and repair, custom fireplace walls, interior and exterior painting, stone walkways and garden borders, and general contracting for residential and commercial spaces.</p><p>The company is based in southwest Houston and operates as a service-area business. There is no public showroom and no street address is published. Estimates happen around the actual project because a photo, room measurement and site conditions are more useful than a staged display.</p><h2>What we do not claim</h2><p>This website does not invent a founding date, license, insurance status, project count, award or review. Those facts remain unpublished until the client verifies them. The same rule applies to photography: gallery images must be original OilerBilt work supplied or approved by the business.</p><h2>Houston conditions are part of the scope</h2><p>Gulf Coast humidity, storm water, freeze-related pipe failures and slab movement change how repair and finish work should be planned. The permitting answer also depends on whether a project is inside Houston, a neighboring municipality or unincorporated Harris County. OilerBilt reviews the address and requested work before making a blanket statement.</p><p><a class="button" href="/free-estimate/">Request an estimate</a></p></article></BaseLayout>
